{"articles":{"Bongaigaon":{"x":"Bongaigaon is an important town (pop: 93,650) in the eastern part of Assam, India. The largest clan of Rashbongshi people in Bongaigaon district is Halua across all Rashbongshi dominated villages.","sights":[{"n":"Bagheswari Hill","k":"see","d":"It is in the middle of the city. From the highest point of the hill you can see a beautiful view of the whole city. There is also a nice Shiv temple on the highest point.","ll":[26.4744,90.5691]},{"n":"Bageshwari temple","k":"see","d":"It is a famous temple for religious in Western Assam.","ll":[26.4726,90.5683]},{"n":"Kakoijana Natural Park","k":"see","d":"It is 15 km away from Bongaigaon city towards the east, covering an area around 20 km².","ll":[26.4312,90.6565]},{"n":"Koya Kujiya Eco Park","k":"see","d":"It is a popular tourist attraction near Abhayapuri about 15 km from Bongaigaon. It attracts thousands of local and foreign tourists every season.","ll":[26.3197,90.6509]},{"n":"Manas National Park","k":"do","d":"Vast wildlife sanctuary, home to protected species such as Bengal tigers, elephants & rhinos.","ll":[26.6595,91.0011]},{"n":"Buddhist Rock Cut Caves","k":"do","d":"The best-preserved relics of the architecture of the Buddhist period.","ll":[26.113,90.7014]}],"c":[11,21,6,13,24,18,17,29,49,21,31,219,24,32,299,26,32,381,26,32,401,26,32,306,25,31,262,22,29,144,17,26,9,13,22,4],"cs":"est"},"Chakdaha":{"x":"Chakdaha, a town in the Nadia district of West Bengal, is the birthplace of woman cricketer Jhulan Goswami, popularly known as the \"Chakdaha Express\".","sights":[{"n":"Calcutta Port Trust Building","k":"see","d":"Simurali was originally developed as a feeder port to Kolkata in the British period. However, the port was later abandoned as the Hooghly River later changed its course.","img":"Calcutta Port Trust building at Simurali, established in British India as a river port of Bhagirathi, in Nadia 28.jpg","ll":[23.04577,88.49982]},{"n":"Jagadish Pandit's Shripat","k":"see","img":"Jagadish Pandit's Sripat along with Jagannath temple at Jasra in Nadia district, West Bengal 14.jpg","ll":[23.07348,88.51172]},{"n":"Palpara Temple","k":"see","d":"A 17th-century terracotta temple, and one of the earliest and rarest surviving examples of the classic char-chala (four-sloped roofs meeting at a pinnacle) style of…","img":"Palpara Temple - South Facade - Nadia 2013-10-20 3676-3687 Archive.tif","ll":[23.05847,88.51695]}],"c":[10,25,11,14,30,19,19,36,32,24,39,59,26,37,165,26,33,244,26,31,342,26,31,301,25,30,238,22,30,148,16,27,23,11,25,11],"cs":"est"},"Dehradun":{"x":"Dehradun is the winter capital of the Indian state of Uttarakhand. Nestled between the Himalayan foothills to the north and the Shivaliks to the south, the town offers breathtaking scenery. It is a favourite destination among tourists, pilgrims and enthusiasts alike from different regions with its serene environment.","sights":[{"n":"The Kalinga War Memorial","k":"see","d":"The only war memorial of its kind in the world which was erected by the British to honour their foe, the Gurkhas (or the Gorkhas).","img":"Anglo Nepali war.jpg","ll":[30.35409,78.08228]},{"n":"The Forest Research Institute Museums","k":"see","d":"Lavish environs and one of the largest institutes of its kind. Guided tours available. Admission free. Museum entry ₹25, covers 6 halls.","img":"Forest Research Institute campus, Dehradun, India.jpg","ll":[30.3439,77.9994]},{"n":"Robber's Cave","k":"see","d":"Robber's cave is a beautiful picnic spot. On display here is one of nature's strange phenomena; a stream of water goes underground here and reappears a few metres away.","img":"Robbers Cave, Dehradun.jpg","ll":[30.3759,78.06092]},{"n":"Chetwoode Hall","k":"see","d":"The Indian Military Academy. A charming little museum housing collections of 20th century military artifacts.","ll":[30.3335,77.9816]},{"n":"Clock Tower","k":"see","d":"Built by the British, this remains the icon of the downtown area.","ll":[30.32434,78.04184]},{