monuments and belongs to the tourist Golden Triangle along with Delhi and Agra.","sights":[{"n":"Amber Fort","k":"see","d":"This massive fort-palace complex built in hybrid Hindu-Muslim style dates back to Raja Man Singh and was the royal palace of the Kachwahas from c. 1600-1727.","img":"Jaipur 03-2016 04 Amber Fort.jpg","ll":[26.98549,75.85134]},{"n":"Dalaram Bagh","k":"see","img":"Dilaram Bagh, Amber 2016.jpg","ll":[26.98625,75.85333]},{"n":"Jaigarh Fort","k":"see","d":"Never conquered in battle, this was considered the strongest of the three forts in the area.","img":"Rajasthan-Jaipur-Jaigarh-Fort-perimeter-walls-Apr-2004-01.JPG","ll":[26.98665,75.84565]},{"n":"Nahargarh Fort","k":"see","d":"The smallest of the three forts, notable primarily for excellent views over Man Sagar lake and the vast sprawl of Jaipur.","img":"Nahargarh fort jaipur.jpg","ll":[26.93995,75.81677]},{"n":"City Palace","k":"see","d":"An imposing blend of traditional Rajput and Mughal architecture. It is a vast palace complex occupying nearly one-seventh of the Pink City.","img":"Jaipur 03-2016 22 City Palace complex.jpg","ll":[26.9255,75.8236]},{"n":"Maota Lake","k":"see","d":"Lake in Rajasthan, India","img":"Amer Fort,Jaipur15.jpg","ll":[26.98333,75.8525],"q":"Q24930625"},{"n":"Jawahar Kala Kendra","k":"see","d":"Cultural center in Jaipur","img":"JKK 08.jpg","ll":[26.8763,75.80917],"q":"Q6165903"},{"n":"Garh Ganesh Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple in Jaipur, India","img":"Jaipur 03-2016 38 Garh Ganesh Temple.jpg","ll":[26.94535,75.82696],"q":"Q5523215"}],"c":[8,22,6,12,26,10,17,32,4,23,38,7,27,41,12,28,40,62,26,35,190,25,33,203,24,34,80,20,34,19,14,30,2,10,25,4],"cs":"imd"},"Jaleswar":{"x":"Jaleswar is a small town in the east of India.","sights":[],"c":[11,24,15,16,28,21,21,33,30,25,37,62,27,36,145,27,33,238,26,31,328,26,31,321,26,30,288,23,30,162,18,27,27,13,24,10],"cs":"est"},"Jaunpur":{"x":"Jaunpur is a city in the Purvanchal part of Eastern Uttar Pradesh. A historical town with Medieval era fort, bridges and mosques. The city was founded by Feroz Shah Tughlaq and named in memory of his cousin, Jaun (popularly known as Muhammad bin Tughluq).","sights":[{"n":"Jaunpur Fort","k":"see","d":"The name Sahi Quila literally translates into royal fort. The fort dates back to the 14th century and was constructed by Ibrahim Naib Barbak, a chieftain of Firoz Shah…","img":"Thomas Daniell - View of the Fort, Jaunpur, Uttar Pradesh.jpg","ll":[25.75023,82.69001]},{"n":"Shahi Bridge","k":"see","d":"A picturesque 16th century bridge across the Gombti which was constructed during Mughal times.","img":"Sahi Bridge 1.jpg","ll":[25.7487,82.68468]},{"n":"Atala mosque","k":"see","d":"The mosque was constructed in 1408 by Ibrahim Shah Sharki. The foundation stone of the mosque was laid by Feorze Shah Tughlaque in 1393.","img":"Shahi Atala Masjid 3.jpg","ll":[25.75276,82.69057]},{"n":"Jaunpur Jami Masjid","k":"see","d":"Built by Hussain Shah Sharqi, the 15th century is one of the largest in India.","img":"Main arcade facade, Jama Masjid, Jaunpur.jpg","ll":[25.75915,82.68503]},{"n":"Char Angul Mosque","k":"see","d":"This small mosque is a hidden gem. It is located deep inside the Mufti Mohalla locality of Jaunpur and is difficult to find.","img":"Char Angul Mosque 3.jpg","ll":[25.7577,82.67244]},{"n":"Shahi Qila","k":"see","d":"Fort in Jaunpur, India","img":"Thomas Daniell - View of the Fort, Jaunpur, Uttar Pradesh.jpg","ll":[25.74975,82.68852],"q":"Q7461611"},{"n":"Lal Darwaza Masjid","k":"see","d":"This Mosque was built in 1447 (as per inscription of this mosque), during the reign of Sultan Mahmud Sharqi, by Queen Bibi Rajyi, dedicated to Maulana Sayyid Ali Dawood…","img":"Lal Darwaza Masjid 03.jpg","ll":[25.77015,82.67149]},{"n":"Jhinjhari Masjid","k":"see","d":"A small and elegant mosque with a towering arched gateway complete with intricate calligraphy from the Koran along with floral and geometric design.","img":"Jhanjhari Masjid 5.jpg","ll":[25.74329,82.70066]}],"c":[8,