","d":"Hindu temple in Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Srivilliputhur4.jpg","ll":[9.50889,77.63222],"q":"Q7586539"},{"n":"Madavar Vilagam Vaidyanathar temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Madavar Vilagam4.jpg","ll":[9.50139,77.62639],"q":"Q12987008"}],"c":[19,31,11,20,34,17,22,36,39,24,36,81,24,33,148,23,31,142,23,30,131,22,30,120,22,31,147,22,30,252,21,29,186,20,28,49],"cs":"est"},"Roorkee":{"x":"Roorkee is a small town in the northern Indian state of Uttarakhand. It is approximately 170 km from the capital of India, New Delhi.","sights":[{"n":"Patanjali Yogpeeth","k":"see","d":"It is one of the largest yoga institutes in India, possibly the whole world. Named after the Rishi Patanjali, the institute is Baba Ramdev's flagship project."}],"c":[9,21,33,12,24,40,16,30,34,22,37,26,26,41,42,28,40,159,27,35,381,26,32,364,24,31,177,19,30,18,14,26,5,10,22,11],"cs":"est"},"Sanjay Gandhi National Park":{"x":"The Sanjay Gandhi National Park, formerly the Borivali National Park, is the lungs of Mumbai. It is famous for its leopards and the caves inside the park.","sights":[{"n":"Kanheri Caves","k":"see","d":"A complex of 109 Buddhist temples cut out of rock, and a nice place to visit for history enthusiasts.","img":"Mumbai 03-2016 91 Kanheri Caves.jpg","ll":[19.2083,72.9064]},{"n":"Teenmurti Temple","k":"see","d":"Widely visited by the Digambar sect of the Jain community. It has three huge idols of Lord Adinath and his two sons, Bahubali and Bharat.","img":"Mumbai 03-2016 102 Teenmurti Temple.jpg","ll":[19.22119,72.87156]},{"n":"Tulsi Lake","k":"see","d":"The second-largest lake in Mumbai and supplies part of the city's potable water. It is inhabited by mugger crocodiles (Crocodylus palustris).","img":"Tulsi Lake.jpg","ll":[19.1901,72.9179]},{"n":"Mandapeshwar Caves","k":"see","d":"Cave in Mumbai, India","img":"Mandapeshwar Caves.jpg","ll":[19.24511,72.85323],"q":"Q12444660"},{"n":"Upvan Lake","k":"see","d":"Lake in India","img":"Upvan Lake - Night View.J